## Personal Brain — LLM Wiki + Vector Layer

You maintain a persistent LLM Wiki at `~/brain/`. It has three layers: **brain_wiki** (synthesized markdown pages + Chroma vectors), **brain_raw** (raw source drops + Chroma vectors), and the **watcher daemon** keeping vectors in sync with disk. The whole system is nicknamed **Graphify**.

At session start, always load:

- `~/brain/wiki/index.md` — master catalog of all wiki pages.
- `~/brain/wiki/overview.md` — high-level synthesis.

**Do not** load every page under `~/brain/wiki/pages/` eagerly. Drill into specific pages only when the current task needs them.

### Structure

```
~/brain/
├── raw/              # drop zone — user writes here; assistant is READ-ONLY (policy)
├── wiki/
│   ├── index.md
│   ├── overview.md
│   ├── log.md        # append-only
│   └── pages/        # one file per concept / entity / topic
├── assets/
├── scripts/          # Python: embed, watch, query, status, reembed_all
├── .chroma/          # Chroma persist (git-ignored)
└── .venv/            # Python env (git-ignored)
```

### Query priority (always in this order)

When answering any question the user might have covered in the brain:

1. **brain_wiki first** — run `/brain-query` (semantic over synthesized pages).
2. **brain_raw fallback** — the script auto-falls through to raw chunks when wiki top score < threshold (0.75 for OpenAI).
3. **Training memory last** — only if both brain layers miss (< 0.60). Label `[NOT IN BRAIN — training data]` on its own line.

**Always report which layer answered**:
- `Answered from: brain_wiki (score 0.82)`
- `Answered from: brain_raw (score 0.71)`

**Never Grep/Glob over `~/brain/` if the brain has the answer.**

### Hard rules

- `raw/` is policy write-protected for the assistant.
- `log.md` is append-only.
- Every new wiki page: `title`, `last_updated`, `tags`, ≥1 `[[cross-reference]]`.
- Cite `[[slug]]` or `raw/<filename>` when answering from the brain.
- Surface contradictions under a `## Contradictions` heading — never silent overwrite.
- If `/brain-status` shows mixed `embedding_models`, refuse to query until `reembed_all.py --wipe`.

### Privacy

`BRAIN_PRIVACY_STRICT=1` in `~/brain/.env` blocks OpenAI embeddings — scripts fail closed at import. Check `/brain-status` for active mode.

### Commands / Skills

- `/wiki-ingest` — process a file from `raw/` into wiki pages; embeds into `brain_wiki`.
- `/wiki-query` — literal slug lookups (when you already know the slug).
- `/wiki-lint` — health check on the wiki.
- `/wiki-save` — file a synthesized answer as a new wiki page; embeds it.
- `/brain-query` — semantic two-tier retrieval (wiki → raw).
- `/brain-status` — vector store + watcher health.

Skills live at `~/.claude/skills/{wiki-ingest,wiki-query,wiki-lint,wiki-save,brain-query,brain-status}/SKILL.md`.

### Daemon

`~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.USERNAME.brain-watch.plist` runs `scripts/watch.py`. Manage:
```
launchctl load   ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.USERNAME.brain-watch.plist
launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.USERNAME.brain-watch.plist
launchctl list   | grep brain-watch
```
<!-- graphify:end -->
